17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186408087 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186408092 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186408094 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1077 "selection" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1079 #edb/ref 17592186408087 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408102 1080 #uuid "d26ace0e-579b-50ca-b6fc-eef06111397d" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408103 1068 #edb/ref 17592186408099 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408103 1069 "q-130322" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408103 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408103 1071 "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408103 1072 #uuid "38a55885-c791-5e66-b4d4-e155d750a7c6" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408103 1074 "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408104 1068 #edb/ref 17592186408098 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408104 1069 "q-275350" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408104 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408104 1071 "Let $r=⟨-4,-1,2⟩$, $q=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $p=⟨5,-2,-1⟩.$ Find $r\\cdot (q\\times p)$ using a determinant.\n\n$r\\cdot (q\\times p)=$\n\n$-21$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408104 1072 #uuid "40346cc1-7283-5552-9863-224be650a17a" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408104 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $r\\cdot (q\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $r,$ $q,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot (q\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)(3\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)+((-2)\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 1)+2((-2)\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =(-4)(-3+2)+(2-5)+2(4-15) \\\\  & =4-3-22 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408105 1068 #edb/ref 17592186408102 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408105 1069 "q-96818" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408105 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408105 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x?$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408105 1072 #uuid "9af6ee75-bad8-5494-acec-5ee5ed4a4af2" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408105 1074 "The notation $g(x)=x$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng:x↦x.\n$$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408106 1068 #edb/ref 17592186408100 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408106 1069 "q-37427" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408106 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408106 1071 "Find all of the subsets of $K={a,c,e}.$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408106 1072 #uuid "d07d1a60-a504-5d37-bfb6-339fef25fc2f" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408106 1074 "To find every subset of $K,$ we list out every combination of elements within $K.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](images/ae/ae24126292e3dbf82d714e1e6f4f6bd2a63b44de2534e29e4ca9ad9b26fbe308.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{a},{c},{e},{a,c},{a,e},{c,e},{a,c,e}.\n$$" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408107 1058 #edb/ref 17592186408113 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408107 1062 #uuid "0ec807ab-037c-5c78-b7f2-ffc5c1ed32df" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408107 1063 #edb/ref 17592186292813 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408108 1058 #edb/ref 17592186408111 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408108 1062 #uuid "1a00c214-df96-503c-a79d-27d6a87a7a2c" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408108 1063 #edb/ref 17592186408106 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408109 1058 #edb/ref 17592186408107 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408109 1062 #uuid "49707255-1ba1-517d-8a23-c980a2f1a1ea" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408109 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097357 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408110 1058 #edb/ref 17592186408114 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408110 1062 #uuid "64f9fdfb-33c0-5218-9ba6-918e895342f8" 13194139533560 17592186045585 true] [17592186408110 1063 #edb/ref 17592186408104 13194139533560 1759218604